          "figure_id": "5.1",
          "caption_text": "Figure 5.1: My experiment: $100 \\times 100$ square grid of houses, $T = 50, 000$ steps of SSPMD, the stepsize policy (5.3.78) with $\\alpha = 20$ . At the resulting solution (¯x, y¯), $\\operatorname{max}_{y \\in \\Delta_{n}}[y^{T} A \\bar{x}] = 0.5016,$ min $[\\bar{y}^{T} Ax] = 0.4985$ x∈∆<sub>n</sub> meaning that the saddle point value is in-between 0.4985 and 0.5016, while the sum of inaccuracies, in terms of the respective objectives, of the primal solution ¯x and the dual solution ¯y is at most $\\epsilon_{\\mathrm{sad}}(\\bar{x}, \\bar{y}) = 0.5016 - 0.4985 = 0.0031$ . It took 1857 sec to compute this solution on my laptop.",
